{"lyrics":"[Intro]\n[00:01.24]Ah\n[00:02.64]The Abyss\n[00:06.40]Ally\n[00:08.28]Mill and Bailey\n[00:10.38]The Abyss, this for y'all\n[Chorus]\n[00:12.28]Drowning in high tide\n[00:15.64]I sit back and watch the time fly\n[00:19.00]Then I pretend that I'm alright\n[00:22.26]Use my hellfire as some sunshine (Shine)\n[Verse 1]\n[00:27.36]Los Angeles, looking at my angles\n[00:30.82]Thanks to Percocets, I almost gave myself a halo\n[00:34.24]Dirty money cleaned by tears, new bankrolls\n[00:37.68]Smoke until my eyes drop tears, then they shut closed\n[00:42.32]I don't know\n[00:43.42]What's going on with me, I don't got time for it, though\n[00:46.42]'Cause I'm too busy roamin' the globe\n[00:48.74]Fly to London for a show, uh\n[00:50.54]Had a luncheon in a castle dungeon, all the dragons calling me bro, oh-woah\n[Interlude]\n[00:53.32]You're in my abyss, there's no escaping\n[00:56.34]There's no hiding\n[01:03.60]This is it, this is all\n[01:06.44]This is the end\n[01:07.64]Hm\n[Verse 2]\n[01:07.70]Woke up from a bad dream, sipped too much Easter pink, oh, yeah\n[01:10.52]My head going off of the brink, oh, yeah\n[01:12.26]Ice on my wrist, hockey rink in here\n[01:13.86]Fresh Prince, but I'm the king, no Bel-Air\n[01:15.38]They hate on me everyday, but I don't care\n[01:17.18]Tryna put negativity up in the air\n[01:18.92]Pray to God that my enemies come to an end\n[01:20.58]It was way more simple when I was a kid\n[Chorus]\n[01:23.20]High tide\n[01:24.22]I sit back and watch the time fly\n[01:27.56]Then I pretend that I'm alright\n[01:30.86]Use my hellfire as some sunshine (Shine)\n[01:37.00]High tide\n[01:37.92]I sit back and watch the time fly\n[01:41.28]Then I pretend that I'm alright\n[01:44.56]Use my hellfire as some sunshine (Shine)","words":[[1.24,2.6,"Ah"],[2.64,2.72,"The"],[2.8,3.2,"Abyss"],[6.4,6.62,"Ally"],[8.28,8.44,"Mill"],[8.54,8.64,"and"],[8.7,9.0,"Bailey"],[10.38,10.48,"The"],[10.58,10.78,"Abyss,"],[10.82,10.9,"this"],[11.32,11.38,"for"],[11.42,11.6,"y